(2) Self-development reading suggestions at this level include: readings on famous military leaders (that is, Grant, Pershing, Patton, Bradley, Ridgeway, Westmoreland and Schwartzkopf); The Five Levels of Leadership, John C. Maxwell.
(3) Self-development educational recommendation. Post secondary education enables Soldiers to develop personal, professional, and occupational skills, as well as increase their career potential, job satisfaction and educational growth. Achievement of an associate’s degree (or 60 semester hours of college) at this level places an individual ahead of their peers. Soldiers should also consider entering a program to gain nationally recognized credentials in an appropriate technical discipline; a list of certifications is available on the COOL Web site.
(4) Self-Development competitive Soldier boards, such as NCO of the Quarter/Year and the SGT Audie Murphy/SGT Morales Clubs broaden the knowledge base, instill discipline, and improve the Soldier’s ability to communicate verbally.', '7653b56d2f08bb1c40e6da9710438fba94b545430f318ca342371fbe45e2c90d', 3, 3, null, 20, null, null, false, null),
