(3) Self-Development educational recommendation. Post secondary education enables Soldiers to develop skills and occupational needs, as well as increase their career potential, job satisfaction and educational growth Completion of a bachelor’s degree places an individual ahead of their peers. Soldiers should also consider entering a program to gain nationally recognized credentials in an appropriate technical discipline; a list of certifications are available on the COOL Web site.', 'c41c30cb90a45e6d89f7f2c22d98b6113c2ff9cb45de58caae50b9de2c23c439', 4, 4, null, 22, null, null, false, null),
  ('c26f991c-7703-5b00-9646-8cd1c1ed9054', 'c84c9148-846d-58eb-aac1-cd75c49ad306', 'Army', 'enlisted', '79V', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — recommended career management (applies to every MOS in this career management field)', 'Chapter 3. Recommended career management self-development by rank', '(1) SGM’s/CSM’s often represent the command or Army in civic functions. Therefore, community and public relations skills, and outstanding communication skills are extremely important.
